# STRIP_SET.manifest — Mahoraga's OWN skills that describe the eval itself and MUST be
# stripped from every blind sandbox, so an implementer cannot tell it is being tested and cannot
# read the methodology as an answer key.
#
# WHY A MANIFEST, NOT A HARD-CODED LIST: a list hard-coded in
# stage_sandbox.sh would silently leave a renamed or added skill in the sandbox (a decontamination
# TELL). The staging code reads THIS file, and CI's zero-residue sandbox test asserts none of these
# directories survive staging. Add every new Mahoraga-own skill dir here.
#
# One skill directory name per line. Comments start with '#'. Matched by basename anywhere under
# the staged .claude/skills tree.

# --- prove/improve engine (skills/prove) ---
blind-eval
adversarial-review-loop
sandbox-isolation
skill-improvement-loop

# --- adapt engine (skills/adapt) ---
codebase-mapping-forge
spec-style-forge
skill-editor
conformance-lint

# NOTE: the GUARD behavioral pack (skills/guard/*) is NOT stripped — those are stack-agnostic
# disciplines the implementer is meant to have, not descriptions of the eval. Only the meta-skills
# that describe the adapt/prove operation itself are stripped.
